# Stripe Integration — Step-by-Step Plan

## How It Works (Big Picture)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User as 📱 User (App)
    participant RN as React Native
    participant Edge as Supabase Edge Function
    participant Stripe as Stripe API
    
    User->>RN: Taps "Pay Now"
    RN->>Edge: POST /stripe-checkout {amount, orderId}
    Edge->>Edge: Verify Clerk JWT
    Edge->>Stripe: stripe.paymentIntents.create({amount, currency: 'idr'})
    Stripe-->>Edge: {clientSecret}
    Edge-->>RN: {clientSecret}
    RN->>RN: initPaymentSheet({clientSecret})
    RN->>RN: presentPaymentSheet()
    User->>Stripe: Enters card → submits
    Stripe-->>RN: ✅ Payment succeeded
    RN->>RN: Save order, clear cart, show success popup
```

---

## Step 1 — Get Your Stripe Keys

**What**: Create a Stripe account and get test-mode API keys.

**How**:
1. Go to [https://dashboard.stripe.com/register](https://dashboard.stripe.com/register) and create an account (or log in)
2. In the dashboard, toggle to **"Test mode"** (top-right switch)
3. Go to **Developers → API keys**
4. Copy two keys:
   - **Publishable key** — starts with `pk_test_...` (this goes in the app)
   - **Secret key** — starts with `sk_test_...` (this goes in the Edge Function, **never** in the app)

**Result**: You have `pk_test_XXXX` and `sk_test_XXXX` ready.

---

## Step 2 — Install Stripe SDK in the App

**What**: Add the `@stripe/stripe-react-native` package to the project.

**How**:
```bash
npm install @stripe/stripe-react-native
```

**Why**: This package gives us:
- `<StripeProvider>` — wraps the app to initialize Stripe
- `useStripe()` — hook with `initPaymentSheet()` and `presentPaymentSheet()`
- The **Payment Sheet** — a pre-built, secure UI for entering card details

**What changes**: Only [`package.json`](file:///c:/Users/ben/Downloads/GymFood-Project/package.json) and `package-lock.json`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> After installing, you'll need to rebuild the native app (`npx expo run:android`) since this package includes native modules.

